          deckDescription: 'One standard 32-card deck: eight ranks (seven through ace) in each of four French suits. No jokers; used for Belote Découverte where part of the hand is exposed and the jack and nine of trump are the two highest cards.',
          suitDescription: 'Four French suits (spades, hearts, diamonds, clubs). Trump is determined by the turned card or bid; follow suit when able. The jack and nine of trump outrank all other trumps; marriages score as in Belote.',
          rankDescription: 'Eight ranks per suit: seven, eight, nine, ten, jack, queen, king, ace. In trump: jack highest, then nine, ace, ten, king, queen, eight, seven. In plain suits: ace, ten, king, queen, jack, nine, eight, seven. Point values follow Belote.',
